Do not claim synchronization or deployment succeeded without evidence.

## 38. Sharing and Publication Protection

Do not change app visibility, sharing permissions, edit permissions, publication settings, or deployment settings without explicit authorization.

Before an authorized sharing or deployment operation, inspect:

- Client-side secret exposure.
- Server-side secret handling.
- API usage and possible costs.
- Authentication requirements.
- Abuse controls.
- User-data access.
- Sharing permissions.
- Operational consequences.

Remember that shared users may be able to view and fork the code. Users with edit permission may modify the application.

Never assume that server-side secret protection means the entire application is secure.

